1
00:00:06,991 --> 00:00:09,581
Whiskers and the Two Left Paws.

2
00:00:18,386 --> 00:00:22,895
One morning, Whiskers' fish came wrapped in a newspaper from Vienna.

3
00:00:23,095 --> 00:00:27,016
Whiskers, look! A Grand Waltz Contest, at the palace in Vienna!

4
00:00:27,216 --> 00:00:30,569
Dancing? No, thank you. I have two left paws.

5
00:00:30,769 --> 00:00:34,804
First prize is the biggest chocolate cake in Vienna. A Sachertorte!

6
00:00:37,693 --> 00:00:40,292
Luna. I have always wanted to dance.

7
00:00:45,332 --> 00:00:48,012
Look! An orchestra bus, going home to Vienna!

8
00:00:57,892 --> 00:00:59,805
Bring me back a crumb of that cake!

9
00:01:05,383 --> 00:01:09,497
So the cats rode to Vienna, inside a double bass case.

10
00:01:18,302 --> 00:01:22,300
Soft velvet, gentle humming... the best bed in the world.

11
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,481
Wake up, Whiskers! The river Danube! And there's Vienna!

12
00:01:32,673 --> 00:01:36,955
Vienna! City of music, palaces, and very fine cake.

13
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:45,997
Good morning, little travellers! Ferdinand, at your service.

14
00:01:46,197 --> 00:01:49,156
Ferdinand, we've come for the Grand Waltz Contest!

15
00:01:49,356 --> 00:01:53,009
At Schönbrunn Palace, tonight! Hop in, I'll show you my city.

16
00:02:02,889 --> 00:02:06,540
That's the Opera. When I was young, I danced at the Riding School!

17
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:10,854
A dancing horse! You can teach me! But first... I smell cake.

18
00:02:14,281 --> 00:02:18,498
Welcome to Café Mitzi! Sachertorte? Apple strudel? Whipped cream?

19
00:02:18,698 --> 00:02:20,657
Yes. Yes. And yes, please!

20
00:02:28,924 --> 00:02:31,719
Whiskers, slow down! We have to practise dancing!

21
00:02:37,297 --> 00:02:40,659
I did that on purpose. It's a, um... cream hat.

22
00:02:40,859 --> 00:02:43,737
Ha! You'll need it. Good luck tonight, my darlings!

23
00:02:46,626 --> 00:02:51,631
Under the giant Ferris wheel in the Prater, Ferdinand gave a dancing lesson.

24
00:02:51,831 --> 00:02:55,023
The waltz is easy. One, two, three. One, two, three.

25
00:03:03,290 --> 00:03:05,616
One, two... ouch! Three... whoops!

26
00:03:12,269 --> 00:03:16,424
It's no good, Luna. At the ball, everyone will laugh at me.

27
00:03:24,154 --> 00:03:27,261
We don't have to go, Whiskers. I don't want you to be sad.

28
00:03:27,461 --> 00:03:31,886
No. You dreamed of this. I'll dance, even if everybody laughs.

29
00:03:38,002 --> 00:03:42,138
That evening, Schönbrunn Palace glowed like a golden cake.

30
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:49,267
A shortcut through the garden! Follow me!

31
00:03:57,534 --> 00:04:00,158
Whiskers, we're lost! The contest is starting!

32
00:04:00,358 --> 00:04:02,761
Wait... I smell chocolate. This way!

33
00:04:07,801 --> 00:04:10,944
The ballroom sparkled with a hundred candles.

34
00:04:11,144 --> 00:04:15,032
Welcome, dancers, to the Grand Waltz! Maestro, if you please!

35
00:04:29,215 --> 00:04:31,295
Oh no. They're all laughing at me.

36
00:04:31,495 --> 00:04:35,760
Forget the counting, Whiskers. Just listen to the music, and hold my paw.

37
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,177
Maestro! Once more, from the beginning!

38
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:55,781
Bravo! That was the happiest waltz this palace has ever seen!

39
00:04:55,981 --> 00:04:58,636
And the prize goes to... Whiskers and Luna!

40
00:05:03,139 --> 00:05:05,959
Cake? Later. Can we dance one more time?

41
00:05:16,915 --> 00:05:21,534
The orchestra bus brought them home, with a very big box of cake.

42
00:05:21,734 --> 00:05:23,701
Whiskers! Can you really dance now?

43
00:05:23,901 --> 00:05:28,173
Two left paws, Pip. But a happy heart. Come on, I'll show you.

44
00:05:37,516 --> 00:05:44,044
Because you don't need perfect steps to dance. You only need the music, a friend, and a happy heart.

